## 12. Value proposition, business model & success measures

- **Value proposition:** for OPD consultants who lose time assembling patient context, the dashboard gives a trusted at-a-glance, source-attributed view in the first seconds of an encounter — unlike facility-bound HMIS summaries, it spans sources and is explicit about gaps. We do **not** claim improved clinical outcomes; no evidence supports that yet.
- **Business model** `[H]`: B2B institutional licence, per-site annual subscription (ACV a hypothesis set by buyer interviews/LOIs). Costs: integration, support, compliance. Sales cycle: owner-led, target < 2 quarters for pilot.

| Measure | Definition & method | Baseline | Target |
|---|---|---|---|
| Time-to-needed-info | Median sec patient-open→review-confirmed; time-motion | Measured in sprint | ≥50% below `[P]` |
| Encounter adoption | % eligible OPD visits summary opened, day 90; logs | 0 at launch | ≥65% `[P]` |
| Information completeness | % encounters no critical item missing; chart audit | Measured | ≥80% `[P]` |
| Wrong-patient opens | Confirmed wrong-patient views; audit+incidents | 0 expected | 0 `[P]` |
| Paid-pilot conversion | Pilot sites → paid contract by month 6 | — | ≥2 of 3 `[P]` |

