## 14. Go-to-market & decision gate

**Pilot approach:** 2–3 private multispecialty clinics; single-specialty wedge within each to limit integration surface; design-partner pricing; co-develop with 1–2 cooperative HMIS vendors.

| Decision | Condition | Outcome |
|---|---|---|
| **PROCEED** | ≥60% clinicians report weekly friction AND baseline measured AND integration feasible ≥2 HMIS AND ≥3 LOIs | Fund MVP; pilot launch ~week 16 |
| **PIVOT** | ≥40% friction but any Proceed condition unmet | HMIS-vendor partnership or narrow to one specialty/facility |
| **STOP** | <40% report friction OR integration infeasible on every HMIS | Cease market activity |

## 15. Strategic recommendations

- **Validated:** the clinician chart-review/EHR time burden (class); India regulatory & interoperability terrain; national digitisation scale.
- **Unvalidated (must test):** India OPD problem magnitude; demand for a separate dashboard; segment counts; willingness to pay.
- **Recommended target:** mid-size private multispecialty clinics, 50–500 OPD/day, HMIS in place.
- **MVP boundary:** read-only, 4 panels, IPS-conformant, in-house records only (external = phase 2).
- **Proceed only if** the gate's four conditions are met; otherwise pivot or stop as defined.
- **Unresolved before build:** root-cause of friction; HMIS API terms; device classification; buyer economics; pending-state reality.

